From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350: let the modem wake the system up

Mark the modem's GLINK edge and its SMP2P edge as wakeup-source, so
that incoming calls, SMS and other QMI indications, and a modem crash,
wake the system up from suspend, as they do on the downstream kernel.

The ADSP, CDSP and SLPI edges stay capable but disabled. Their traffic
during suspend (battery status, sensors) can be enabled from user space
where it is wanted.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
Built with W=1 and dtbs_check; not tested on the device yet.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi
index e32505c..3fe539d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi
@@ -616,6 +616,8 @@
 		qcom,local-pid = <0>;
 		qcom,remote-pid = <1>;
 
+		wakeup-source;
+
 		smp2p_modem_out: master-kernel {
 			qcom,entry-name = "master-kernel";
 			#qcom,smem-state-cells = <1>;
@@ -2544,6 +2546,7 @@
 						IPCC_MPROC_SIGNAL_GLINK_QMP>;
 				label = "modem";
 				qcom,remote-pid = <1>;
+				wakeup-source;
 			};
 		};
 
